From: RK3128 reference <reference@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: rockchip: describe boot logo reservation

Describe the optional named reservation used by the RK3128 reference board DRM takeover.

Signed-off-by: RK3128 reference <reference@example.invalid>
---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/rockchip/rockchip-vop.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/rockchip/rockchip-vop.yaml
@@ -77,9 +77,25 @@
   iommus:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  memory-region:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      Reserved bootloader scan-out memory. On RK3128 reference board the VOP driver
+      returns the pages to the allocator after a verified DRM takeover.
+      The region must remain reserved until then and must not have no-map
+      or reusable set.
+
+  memory-region-names:
+    items:
+      - const: boot-logo
+
   power-domains:
     maxItems: 1
 
+dependentRequired:
+  memory-region: [memory-region-names]
+  memory-region-names: [memory-region]
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
